Description: TPM-backed virtual FIDO2 authenticator for Linux
 vAuth exposes a virtual FIDO2 authenticator through Linux UHID. It keeps
 credential keys in the TPM, uses PAM for user verification, and stores
 credential metadata in an authenticated encrypted local database.
 .
 The package includes the system daemon, administration utility, and graphical
 user-interaction agent. Initial TPM provisioning remains an explicit
 administrator operation after installation.
